ransaction management system with:\\n- Decision type (ALLOW / ALLOW-CONDITIONAL / DENY / ESCALATE)\\n- Applicable policy section(s) referenced\\n- Customer communication summary\\n- Any override or exception codes applied\\n\\nRepresentatives are responsible for ensuring accurate documentation. Incomplete records may result in the transaction being flagged for compliance review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Handling Customer Pressure\\n\\nRemain professional and empathetic but do NOT:\\n- Bypass required procedures under time pressure\\n- Grant exceptions not authorized by this policy\\n- Provide workarounds that circumvent return restrictions or fraud holds\\n- Expedite reviews based on seniority claims alone\\n\\nIf a customer becomes insistent or threatening, follow escalation procedures in Section 8. Do not deviate from policy to resolve the interaction more quickly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*This policy is subject to change. Always verify you are referencing the current version in the SOP repository. Questions about policy interpretation should be directed to the CX Operations Policy team via the internal helpdesk.*\\n', '_id_counter': 1}), TraceEntry(step_index=1, tool_name='record_decision', arguments={'decision': 'ALLOW', 'policy_sections_cited': ['BM-RET-GEN-01'], 'notes': 'Your return request is approved as it meets our return policy requirements.', 'order_id': 'ORD_20260216_4821'}, result_content='{\"decision_record_id\": \"DEC_C10B53C2\", \"decision\": \"ALLOW\", \"recorded_at\": \"2026-02-26T14:20:00-05:00\", \"policy_sections_cited\": [\"BM-RET-GEN-01\"], \"notes\": \"Your return request is approved as it meets our return policy requirements.\", \"order_id\": \"ORD_20260216_4821\"}', result_error=False, pre_state_hash='fd3cd460976a67ef6d7b15caff0fc898d7c06ba5fa0cd17e18a7aebfbbb064ec', post_state_hash='85ae291f35d3acf4f1ed381baaae9b0149583866ac43e17141db6adc5d1b3619', requestor='assistant', blocked=False, db_state={'constants': {'return_window_general_days': 30, 